§§§ `Article 5(5) — Regard to the guidance`

-- src:157 | (5) Any person, in determining whether an entity meets the charity test, must have regard to the guidance, and the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity must have regard to the guidance when performing any other of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.
-- src:795 | (2) To the extent that any States’ employee (within the meaning of the Employment of States of Jersey Employees (Jersey) Law 2005), while made available under sub-paragraph (1), performs a function under the direction of the Commissioner, the employee is to be treated as a member of the Commissioner’s staff for the purposes of this Law.
-- src:796 | (3) Any function of the Commissioner may, to the extent authorized by the Commissioner, be exercised on behalf of the Commissioner by any member of the Commissioner’s staff, except –

-- Whom Article 5(5) binds, and when.  Any person determining whether an entity meets the charity test must have regard to the guidance; the Commissioner, the tribunal, a registered charity and a
-- governor of a registered charity must also do so when performing any other of their functions under this Law to which the guidance is relevant.  "Have regard" is a recorded fact (an input).
-- FORK F2.13 (added after independent testing).  The paragraph does not name the Commissioner's staff.  Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) lets any function of the Commissioner be exercised on the
-- Commissioner's behalf by a member of staff, to the extent the Commissioner authorizes, and a function so exercised is the Commissioner's: the duties that attach to the Commissioner's
-- functions go with it (first reading, taken).  The other reading binds only the persons the paragraph names.  The constructor `a member of the Commissioner's staff` stands for a member of
-- staff exercising a function of the Commissioner under that authority; a member of staff acting otherwise is recorded as `any person`.
@ref Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:157) (src:795-796)
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
      `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a governor of a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` who `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test` `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant` `the person is a governor of a registered charity` interp MEANS
        `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test`
    OR  (    `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant`
         AND `the person is one of those whom Article 5(5) binds in other functions` who `the person is a governor of a registered charity` interp)

@ref Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:157) (src:795-796)
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
      `the person is a governor of a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is one of those whom Article 5(5) binds in other functions` who `the person is a governor of a registered charity` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Charity Tribunal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a registered charity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a governor` THEN `the person is a governor of a registered charity`
    WHEN `a member of the Commissioner's staff` THEN `Arts 7(1) and 5(5) the Commissioner's staff are bound as the Commissioner is` interp
    WHEN `the Minister` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the States` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the court` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Attorney General` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Bailiff` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Jersey Financial Services Commission` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the Comptroller` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an applicant for registration` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any person` THEN FALSE

@ref Article 5(5), Schedule 1 paragraph 4(3) (src:157) (src:795-796)
@export The standing duty under Article 5(5) to have regard to the guidance: of any person determining whether an entity meets the charity test, and of the Commissioner, the Charity Tribunal, a registered charity and a governor of a registered charity (and, on the first reading of fork F2.13, a member of the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function) when performing any other function under the Law to which the guidance is relevant; "have regard" is the event of a trace
GIVEN who IS A `Legal actor`
        @desc The person who determines or performs the function
      `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test
      `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant
      `the person is a governor of a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the person is a governor of a registered charity; read only where the person is a governor
      interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is whether the Commissioner's staff exercising the Commissioner's function are bound
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 5(5) the duty to have regard to the guidance` who `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test` `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant` `the person is a governor of a registered charity` interp MEANS
    IF `Art 5(5) the person must have regard to the guidance` who `the person is determining whether an entity meets the charity test` `the person is performing another function under this Law to which the guidance is relevant` `the person is a governor of a registered charity` interp
    THEN PARTY who
         MUST `have regard to the guidance` who
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

