§§§ `Article 5(6) — Consultation and a report before issuing or amending guidance`

-- src:158 | (6) Before issuing or amending guidance the Commissioner must –
-- src:159 | (a) consult –
-- src:160 | (i) any persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes,
-- src:161 | (ii) the Minister, and
-- src:162 | (iii) such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate; and
-- src:163 | (b) publish a report on the Commissioner’s views on the results of the consultation, and the reasons for the Commissioner’s decision on the guidance in the light of those results.

-- Which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) reach.  FORK F2.12: the guidance under 5(4), with the guidance on public benefit that 7(4) requires it to contain (first reading, taken), or any
-- guidance the Commissioner issues or amends (second).  The first is supported by Article 11(6)(b), which makes Articles 5(6) to (8) "apply to that guidance as they apply to guidance under
-- Article 5(4)": that provision would be unnecessary if they already reached all guidance.  Guidance that covers several subjects is in scope on the first reading if any of them is a 5(4) subject.
-- The rules of 5(6) to 5(8) below do not read this: ask it first; they assume the guidance is in scope.
@ref Article 5(6), Article 5(7), Article 5(8) (src:158-165)
@export Whether Articles 5(6) to 5(8) (consultation, report, copy to the Minister, laying before the States) apply to guidance on the given subjects: on the first reading only guidance under Article 5(4) and its public benefit content, on the second any guidance the Commissioner issues or amends
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to
      `the subjects of the guidance issued or amended` IS A LIST OF `Subject of the Commissioner's guidance`
        @desc The subjects the guidance covers; one document may cover several
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(6) Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to the guidance` interp `the subjects of the guidance issued or amended` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `which guidance Articles 5(6) to 5(8) apply to`
    WHEN `the guidance under Article 5(4), including the guidance on public benefit that Article 7(4) requires it to contain`
        THEN   elem `the determination of whether an entity meets the charity test` `the subjects of the guidance issued or amended`
            OR elem `the determination of whether an entity provides or intends to provide public benefit` `the subjects of the guidance issued or amended`
    WHEN `any guidance that the Commissioner issues or amends` THEN TRUE

-- 5(6)(a): consult (i) any persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or of bodies with charitable purposes, (ii) the Minister, and (iii) such other persons as the
-- Commissioner considers appropriate.  Whom the Commissioner considers representative or appropriate is the Commissioner's opinion: it is the pair of inputs below.
@ref Article 5(6)(a) (src:159-162)
GIVEN `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult` IS A BOOLEAN
      `persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative were consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate were consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult` `persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative were consulted` `the Minister was consulted` `such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate were consulted` MEANS
        "(i)" ... (    NOT `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes`
                   OR `persons appearing to the Commissioner to be representative were consulted`)
    AND "(ii)" ... `the Minister was consulted`
    AND "(iii)" ... (    NOT `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult`
                     OR `such other persons as the Commissioner considers appropriate were consulted`)

-- 5(6) as a chain of duties: consult as (a) requires; then publish a report on the Commissioner's views on the results of the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance
-- (b).  Neither names a period of its own: each is to be done before the guidance is issued or amended, which `Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` tests.
@ref Article 5(6) (src:158-163)
@export The Commissioner's duty under Article 5(6), before issuing or amending guidance, to consult those whom Article 5(6)(a) names and then publish a report on the views on the consultation and the reasons for the decision; the consultation event must cover them, and the duty has no deadline of its own
GIVEN `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or of bodies with charitable purposes
      `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`Art 5(6) the Commissioner must consult and publish a report before issuing or amending guidance` `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `consult` `the Commissioner` representatives minister others
    PROVIDED `Art 5(6)(a) the consultation covered those whom Article 5(6)(a) names` `any persons appear to the Commissioner to be representative of charities or bodies with charitable purposes` `the Commissioner considers that there are other persons whom it is appropriate to consult` representatives minister others
    HENCE (   PARTY `the Commissioner`
              MUST `publish a report on the views on the consultation and the reasons for the decision on the guidance` `the Commissioner`
              HENCE FULFILLED)

-- FORK F2.7 ("Before issuing or amending guidance"): the consultation and the report must precede the day the guidance is issued or amended (strictly earlier, taken) or may fall on that day.
-- Either way the consultation must not come after the report, because the report is "on the Commissioner's views on the results of the consultation".  A date not yet reached is NOTHING.
@ref Article 5(6) (src:158-163)
@export Whether the Commissioner consulted and published the report before issuing or amending the guidance, on the reading of "before" chosen by the interpretation; the consultation may not come after the report
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
        @desc The readings of the ambiguous provisions of Articles 3 to 7; the field read here is how "before issuing or amending guidance" is read
      `the date the guidance was issued or amended` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the guidance was issued or amended
      `the date the consultation was held` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the consultation required by Article 5(6)(a) was held; NOTHING if it has not been held
      `the date the report was published` IS A MAYBE DATE
        @desc The day the report required by Article 5(6)(b) was published; NOTHING if it has not been published
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(6) the consultation and the report preceded the guidance` interp `the date the guidance was issued or amended` `the date the consultation was held` `the date the report was published` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the consultation was held`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST consulted
        THEN CONSIDER `the date the report was published`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST reported
                 THEN `Art 5(6) the dates fall in the order Article 5(6) requires` interp consulted reported `the date the guidance was issued or amended`

@ref Article 5(6) (src:158-163)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      consulted IS A DATE
      reported IS A DATE
      issued IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(6) the dates fall in the order Article 5(6) requires` interp consulted reported issued MEANS
        consulted AT MOST reported
    AND `Art 5(6) the day precedes the issue of the guidance` interp consulted issued
    AND `Art 5(6) the day precedes the issue of the guidance` interp reported issued

@ref Article 5(6) (src:158-163)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      day IS A DATE
      issued IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(6) the day precedes the issue of the guidance` interp day issued MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how before issuing or amending guidance is read`
    WHEN `the consultation and the report must fall on an earlier day than the day the guidance is issued or amended` THEN day LESS THAN issued
    WHEN `the consultation and the report may fall on the day the guidance is issued or amended` THEN day AT MOST issued

