    CONSIDER interp's `how the days of a measured period are counted`
    WHEN `the day of the event is not counted, so the day after it is the first day` THEN days
    WHEN `the day of the event is the first day` THEN days MINUS 1

-- Whether an act on a given day falls within a period measured in days from the day of an event: not before the event, and not after the last day.
@ref Article 5(7), Article 5(8) (src:164) (src:165)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      event IS A DATE
      act IS A DATE
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 5(7) and 5(8) the act falls within the days counted from the event` interp event act days MEANS
        (Day act MINUS Day event) AT LEAST 0
    AND (Day act MINUS Day event) AT MOST `Art 5(7) and 5(8) the number of days after the event within which the act is in time` interp days

-- Reading A of 5(7): no period is stated, so the duty stands until performed.
@ref Article 5(7) (src:164)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Articles 3 to 7`
`reading A of Article 5(7): no period is stated` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST `provide to the Minister a copy of the issued or amended guidance and the report` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Reading B of 5(7): within the number of days that counts as a reasonable time, counted from the day the guidance was issued or amended.
